# Default fallback goal — used when prompts/goal.txt is marked complete
# (first line: "GOAL_STATUS: complete") and no replacement goal has been
# set yet. wake.sh substitutes this file in for that session only; it does
# not overwrite goal.txt.
#
# Copy this to prompts/default_goal.txt. The template below is a reasonable
# default for most nodes — edit it if your agent should behave differently
# when it finds itself between goals.

GOAL_STATUS: active

No active goal is currently assigned. The previous goal was marked complete
and no replacement has been set yet.

Use this session productively within the boundaries of your assigned session
type:
- If Loom has scheduled or needs_plan tasks, work those instead of treating
  this as a free session — check state/loom_context.json first.
- If the queue is genuinely empty, this is a legitimate maintenance/
  reflection session: review recent memory files, check system health, or
  (if philosophy sessions are enabled) use the time for identity/
  relationship work.
- Do not invent a new primary goal on your own. Assigning the next one is
  the owner's call. Note in memory/latest_summary.md that a new goal is
  needed, and surface it to the owner via whatever communication channel
  is configured.
